## Why This Is Asked

This question tests balancing reliability and speed in a multi-team setting with a live data pipeline. It pushes candidates to articulate ownership, metrics, and governance for a delicate system upgrade.

## Key Concepts

- Event-driven architecture, exactly-once delivery, idempotency
- Cross-team ownership & governance, capacity planning
- Dual-track planning, go/no-go gates, risk mitigation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example idempotent handler
function handleEvent(event) {
  const id = event.id;
  if (hasProcessed(id)) return;
  markProcessed(id);
  process(event);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure success and adapt if MTTR targets aren’t met?
- What would trigger a rollback vs. feature flag deprecation in production?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests programmatic planning and cross‑team coordination for a high‑risk migration that must preserve reliability while delivering features. It also probes governance, risk controls, and measurable progress.

## Key Concepts
- Phased migration with canary and blue/green patterns
- Cross‑team ownership: telemetry, incident management, deployment
- Acceptance criteria, Definition of Ready, gate reviews
- Reliability metrics (SLOs), rollback strategies, and feature flags

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: canary flag check
if (featureFlags.canaryEnabled(service)) {
  routeToCanary(service);
} else {
  routeToStable(service);
}
